@startuml Topic5_Orchestrator_Role
' ============================================================
' TOPIC 5: The Orchestrator Role (the manager / conductor)
' COORDINATES, does NOT execute. Subagents do the work.
' 3 functions: Decompose -> Assign -> Aggregate (validate!).
' ============================================================
title Topic 5 — The Orchestrator Role\n(COORDINATES, does NOT execute — the manager/conductor)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 12

start

:Complex task arrives at the ORCHESTRATOR;
note right
  Orchestrator = manager/conductor.
  It COORDINATES the work but does
  NOT do the work itself.
  Maps to a HUB-AND-SPOKE topology
  (hub = orchestrator, spokes = subagents).
end note

partition "1. DECOMPOSE" {
  :Break task into BOUNDED subtasks;
  note right
    Each subtask must be small,
    well-scoped, independently doable.
  end note
}

partition "2. ASSIGN" {
  :Hand each subtask to a chosen subagent;
  note right
    Orchestrator ASSIGNS the work.
    Subagents NEVER self-select their jobs.
  end note
}

partition "3. AGGREGATE" {
  :Collect subagent outputs;
  #Yellow:**VALIDATE** each result;
  note right
    VALIDATE is the FORGOTTEN step.
    Don't blindly trust subagent output —
    check it before combining.
  end note
  :Synthesize into one coherent result;
}

if (Any subagent failed / bad result?) then (YES)
  #LightBlue:Apply ERROR HANDLING (see note);
  note right
    == ERROR HANDLING lives in the ORCHESTRATOR ==
    1. **RETRY** — same subagent, same task, try again
    2. **SUBSTITUTE** — different subagent/tool/approach,
       SAME goal
    3. **ESCALATE** — hand UP to a human
       (e.g. at an authorization boundary)
  end note
else (NO)
  #LightGreen:Return final synthesized answer;
endif

stop

floating note left
  == ORCHESTRATOR HOLDS 4 THINGS ==
  1. **Master plan** — the intended strategy / roadmap
  2. **Execution state** — current reality (what's done so far)
  3. **Error logic** — retry / substitute / escalate rules
  4. **Aggregation rules** — how to validate & merge results
  ....
  Master plan (intended) vs Execution state (actual)
  are DIFFERENT — plan is the map, state is where you are.
  ----
  Substitute vs Escalate:
  * Substitute = still solvable by the system another way
  * Escalate = needs a human (authority / judgment / missing info)
end note

@enduml
